  displayName: Scorched rhyme sheet
  description: A children's rhyme, half burnt. 'The Tallyman, the Tallyman, he weighs
    the rain, he counts the sand. He'll buy your coat, he'll buy your name, he'll
    wear a friend's face when he came. But gifts are gifts and can't be bought, so
    give him nothing. Give him naught.'
